// {2}{R} instant: "~ deals 3 damage to any target unless that player pays
// {2}." — the `Reference::Coalesce` fixture. The resolution-time toll
// ([CR#118.12a], the collapsed `May(Pay(cost))` MustPay shape) names a
// SINGLE payer that is derived one of two ways from an `AnyTarget` slot
// ([CR#115.4]): a permanent's controller ([CR#109.4]), or — when the target
// IS a player — that player directly. `Coalesce([ControllerOf(Target(0)),
// Target(0)])` is exactly that "first non-null payer" read (proven both
// branches in resolve::query::tests). No real card in canon/testing/builtin
// carries the coalesced-payer shape (the only one, Rhystic Lightning, lives
// in the generated plugins/wizards, which the no-dead-grammar gate does not
// count), so this mock isolates it end to end (parse -> render -> engine).
Normal(
    name: "Rhystic-toll DealDamage",
    mana_cost: [Generic(2), Red],
    types: [Instant],
    abilities: [
        Spell(effect: Targeted(
            targets: [AnyTarget],
            effect: May(
                who: Coalesce([ControllerOf(Target(0)), Target(0)]),
                effect: Pay([Mana([Generic(2)])]),
                if_not: DealDamage(This, 3, Target(0)),
            ),
        )),
    ],
)
